<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/10th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Trans</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">939</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Trans was fought in 939 at Trans, near Dol in north-eastern Brittany, traditionally on 1 August. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alan-ii-duke-of-brittany">Alan Twisted Beard</a>, who had returned from exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, defeated the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> army in Brittany. The victory completed the expulsion of the Norsemen who had occupied the region since the early 10th century and restored Breton rule under Alan as duke.</p></div>
